"""JSP-Oct26-Search-Escape; ©2026 ThomasB. Report measured prototype evidence."""
import pathlib,json,sys,shutil,datetime,hashlib
source=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);dest=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2]);dest.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=False)
s=json.loads((source/'screen-v6/summary.json').read_text());assert len(s['trials'])==14
shutil.copytree(source/'screen-v6',dest/'swift-screen')
for name in ['cpsat4.json','cpsat11.json','cpsat-neighborhoods.json','cpsat-global.json']:shutil.copy2(source/name,dest/name)
shutil.copytree(source/'native-exact4',dest/'native-exact4')
lines=['# JSP-Oct26-Search-Escape-Report','','©2026 ThomasB','','Author: ThomasB','',f'Generated {datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat()}. This report precedes live integration.','', '**No original-puzzle solve occurred in the 14 Swift screening trials. All retained 14 wrong clues and residual 0.17078227.** The mechanisms changed measurable behavior, while CP-SAT independently improved residual to 0.16036970 in one small neighborhood. No solve-time superiority is established.','','## Local Swift screen','','Original 11×11, same archived incumbent, four cooperating CPU threads, two matched seeds, 30 seconds per policy. Trial order reverses in the second block. The control is the new harness using the legacy persistent-BP scheduler and best-only exchange, not a rerun of the original production architecture. Probe clocks are accelerated to 3/8/16 seconds; live settings are 60/180/600. No discoveries cross policies. All final partitions and worker partitions passed independent Python validation.','','| Policy | Distinct legal boards published, seeds 1 / 2 | Protected BP nodes, seeds 1 / 2 | Wrong clues, both |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for name in s['config']['policies']:
 rows=[r for r in s['trials'] if r['policy']==name]
 lines.append(f'| {name} | '+ ' / '.join(str(r['distinctPublished']) for r in rows)+' | '+' / '.join(str(r['repairs'].get('protectedNodes',0)) for r in rows)+' | 14 |')
lines+=['','Distinct published boards count canonical legal partitions observed by the archive, including candidates not retained. Active walks were already distinct in the control; the diversity change expands sharing and working-basin choices. Protected-node counts are executed work, not completion percentages. The combined trial includes one exact-feasibility lane. Candidate states differ between policies after initialization by design.','','Both escalation probes created full-board protected jobs and scopes of at least 32 cells. Diversity runs performed 8–9 migrations. Adaptive/recombination runs actually exercised different scope kinds, but 30 seconds is insufficient to rank all operators. Most adaptive time initially goes to neighbor/full-board work. These are composite experimental policies, not a complete factorial study.','','CPU use ranged from %.2f to %.2f equivalents. Local build/tests and the one-thread CP-SAT probes briefly overlapped this short screen; throughput and hardware timing must not be treated as controlled speed comparisons. The original Mini run stayed active throughout. Timing includes loading and checkpoint I/O. Raw inputs, outputs, counters, binary hash and source snapshot accompany this report.'%(min(r['cpuEquivalentCores'] for r in s['trials']),max(r['cpuEquivalentCores'] for r in s['trials'])),'','## Independent constraint approach','']
cp4=json.loads((source/'cpsat4.json').read_text());native=json.loads((source/'native-exact4/result.json').read_text());patches=json.loads((source/'cpsat-neighborhoods.json').read_text());best=min((r for r in patches if r['quality']),key=lambda r:(r['quality']['wrong'],r['quality']['residual']));glob=json.loads((source/'cpsat-global.json').read_text())
lines += [f'- On the same generated 4×4 fixture, native exact BP solved in {native["seconds"]:.3f} s; CP-SAT solved in {cp4["seconds"]:.3f} s including {cp4["catalogSeconds"]:.3f} s to generate all {cp4["candidateShapes"]} legal shapes. One small case validates functionality, not a general speed ranking. No uniqueness claim.',f'- Eight original-puzzle neighborhoods of 12–16 cells used exhaustive local shape domains with the exterior fixed. Best: 14 wrong clues, residual {best["quality"]["residual"]:.8f}, in {best["seconds"]:.3f} s including preparation. All returned labels and shortest distances were independently checked. This improves residual by {(1-best["quality"]["residual"]/.17078226998999335)*100:.2f}%, with no reduction in wrong clues.',f'- A whole-board restricted domain of {glob["candidateShapes"]} shapes ran for {glob["seconds"]:.2f} s and returned {glob["status"]}, 14 wrong clues with unchanged residual. The domain uses rectangles and transformed incumbent regions and is incomplete; no original-puzzle infeasibility conclusion follows.','- CP-SAT minimizes wrong-clue count followed by absolute distance error. The retained Swift objective uses normalized residual as its secondary criterion. Candidate acceptance uses independent original-quality evaluation; the differing secondary objective is explicit.','- Model constraints enforce exact-cover symmetric regions, capital rules, integer state sizes, positive edge weights and Bellman equalities for shortest distances. Path inequalities alone are not used as an exact-distance substitute.','','## Decisions backed by this screen','','1. Integrate canonical alternative sharing and separate working-basin references: observed diversity and migrations increased without losing the incumbent. This is a mechanism result, not proof of faster solving.','2. Integrate explicit scope growth, protected CPU service, compatible stack restoration and exhausted-scope memoization. The broad searches received real nodes; default full-board work is bounded rather than assigned to every worker.','3. Keep adaptive operators/recombination enabled in an experimental portfolio with telemetry and exploration. Their solve benefit remains unproven; do not replace all neighbor repairs or privilege routes.','4. Reserve one Mini thread for persistent exact feasibility, while retaining heuristic workers. Native small-case solving passed, but the target did not solve in the short screen.','5. Run CP-SAT as an optional one-core local sidecar performing exact small-neighborhood repair, with occasional restricted full-board search. It is the only screened approach to produce a better retained target candidate. Exchange only validated puzzle-matched states.','','## Next implementation and validation','','Add protected stack recovery across segments, pool-wide stagnation clocks, current/retained energy and diversity telemetry, compatible checkpoint checks and an independent local CP-SAT sidecar. Preserve the stopped v5 run and its final/checkpoint data before a version-6 standalone restart. The live target is a solve attempt, not another short timing comparison. No fan controls or installed production executable are changed.','','References: [Large Neighborhood Search](https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5293785/Pisinger.pdf), [official CP-SAT guide](https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver).']
(dest/'JSP-Oct26-Search-Escape-Report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
manifest={str(p.relative_to(dest)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in dest.rglob('*') if p.is_file()}
(dest/'JSP-Oct26-Search-Escape-Evidence.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(experiment='JSP-Oct26-Search-Escape',copyright='©2026 ThomasB',author='ThomasB',artifacts=manifest),indent=2))
print(dest/'JSP-Oct26-Search-Escape-Report.md')
